Since, $\left[\begin{array}{cc}\alpha & \beta \\ \gamma & -\alpha\end{array}\right]$ is a square root of $I_2$ i.e. two rowed unit matrix.
$\therefore \quad\left[\begin{array}{cc}\alpha & \beta \\ \gamma & -\alpha\end{array}\right]^2=\left[\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right]\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & {\left[\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}\alpha & \beta \\ \gamma & -\alpha\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}{cc}\alpha & \beta \\ \gamma & -\alpha\end{array}\right]} \\ \Rightarrow & {\left[\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{ll}\alpha^2+\beta \gamma & \alpha \beta-\alpha \beta \\ \gamma \alpha-\gamma \alpha & \gamma \beta+\alpha^2\end{array}\right]}\end{array}
$\Rightarrow \quad\left[\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}\alpha^2+\beta_\gamma & 0 \\ 0 & \alpha^2+\beta_\gamma\end{array}\right]\begin{aligned} & \therefore \quad \alpha^2+\beta \gamma=1 \\ & \Rightarrow 1-\alpha^2-\beta \gamma=0\end{aligned}
